      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0",
      "artist": "No machine-readable author provided. Imus Eus assumed (based on copyright claims).",
      "description": "Das Rote Haus in Monschau - an der Mündung des Laufenbachs in die Rur. Es wurde um 1760 von dem Tuchverleger Johann Heinrich Scheibler erbaut und vereint Wohn- und Arbeitsräume (Kontor, Wolllager, Wollspüle, Färberei) unter einem Dach. Foto: 2008\n\nThe Red House in Monschau near Aachen - built by the cloth manufacturer Johann Heinrich Scheibler around 1760 - shows upper class domestic life. The house was not only used as a family residence, but also housed the offices and storage rooms, not forgetting the cellar with its scouring and dying rooms and their rinsing channels. 2008",
